Third-party material
--------------------

The official VDA 5050 JSON schemas, vendored under:

  backend/app/schemas/vda5050-2.1.0/  (tag 2.1.0, commit 511d01d71587e8a3dc5e71d4f41dc52466f4284c)
  backend/app/schemas/vda5050-3.0.0/  (tag 3.0.0, commit e9ba560b0e2d3f66526550ad5d61b8a2ad936172)

are copyright Verband der Automobilindustrie and licensed under the MIT License.
Source: https://github.com/VDA5050/VDA5050
The full MIT license text is in LICENSE.txt inside each of those folders.

The 2.1.0 files are unchanged from upstream. In the 3.0.0 files factsheet.schema, order.schema and
visualization.schema, 7 trailing commas (invalid JSON) were removed; nothing else was changed
(see backend/app/schemas/README.md).

The optional ROS 2 robot (ros2/, D-51) is built from third-party open-source code fetched at image build time,
not included in this repository: InOrbit's vda5050_connector (https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop) and
vda5050_adapter_examples (https://github.com/inorbit-ai/vda5050_adapter_examples), BSD-3-Clause; ROS 2, Nav2 and
TurtleBot3 packages from the ROS distribution (Apache-2.0 and BSD licences).
